diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b1234d7..17040b5 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@ The PiG user website adapts the information architecture of pi.dev. It uses Reac
 - Upstream release data is adapted from the MIT-licensed Pi project and remains labeled as upstream content.
 - News comes from PiG's GitHub releases, read at `pnpm generate` by `scripts/fetch-releases.mjs` into `data/pig-releases.json` (not committed), which also feeds `feed.xml`. With no releases or no access, News shows an empty state. The daily deploy picks up new releases.
 - The model catalog in `data/models.json` is generated from the pinned Pi package's published catalog by `scripts/site-models.mjs` (`pnpm models:build`), the same source as PiG's Go catalog.
-- The catalog lists npm packages by keyword: Pi packages (`pi-package`), PiG packages (`pig-package`) and Piglets (`pig-piglet`). `scripts/build-npm-catalog.mjs` reads npm search at `pnpm generate`, falls back to the committed `data/npm-catalog.snapshot.json` when npm fails, and writes ignored `public/catalog/*.json`. The 27 reviewed packages in `data/verified-packages.json` carry a "Verified with PiG" badge; their historical smoke checks used the unreleased `0.2.1+0.87.1`. `scripts/build-package-catalog.mjs` projects them into ignored `data/packages.public.json`. See [docs/catalog-sync.md](docs/catalog-sync.md).
+- The catalog first lists what the Pigpen repository has released (Packages from Git tags, signed Piglet Binaries from GitHub Releases; `scripts/build-pigpen-catalog.mjs`), then npm packages by keyword: Pi packages (`pi-package`), PiG packages (`pig-package`) and Piglets (`pig-piglet`). `scripts/build-npm-catalog.mjs` reads npm search at `pnpm generate`, falls back to the committed `data/npm-catalog.snapshot.json` when npm fails, and writes ignored `public/catalog/*.json`. The 27 reviewed packages in `data/verified-packages.json` carry a "Verified with PiG" badge; their historical smoke checks used the unreleased `0.2.1+0.87.1`. `scripts/build-package-catalog.mjs` projects them into ignored `data/packages.public.json`. See [docs/catalog-sync.md](docs/catalog-sync.md).
 - The UI uses Grommet components and a project-owned theme.
 
 ### Navigation and package catalogs
